ust  trying out random stuff and i recorded  all of it anyway so i figured  it's gonna be a messy video but i might  as well throw everything into a video  and see what i can make of it  and this build i think was worth showing  off because  well in the last video i made venice and  i was really sad about how  saint mark's bell tower on the central  plaza  just looked not very convincing built on  a single grid space  so i figured it's a decently simple  building really um with colors that are  all in the game  so it should probably be possible to  recreate it in the game at least  somewhat believably and well looking at  the tower structure itself i guess  that's partly true because you can  definitely  build the uh the red section the lower  section of the tower and then  going into the the white part at the top  pretty  convincingly but i totally forgot that  there's no good  piece in the game for the roof so yeah  to be fair  i do think the roof ends up looking a  little bit derpy in the end  especially given the fact that it's just  some green walls and then  still the orange roof on top of that so  it's a kind of strange structure  but it's recognizable and i think  sometimes i have to scale down my  expectations a little bit and realize  that this game isn't meant for this kind  of stuff at all and  the fact that you can achieve this very  easily and very quickly without having  to  you know work at the game too much just  by doodling around  it's uh it's pretty cool and it's still  pretty fun to build  so i'm very happy with the final results  and let's just check it out for a second  so here's the end result it's not the  best thing i've ever made but it was  pretty fun to build  and i guess it's recognizable and i made  it very quickly so  i can't really be too disappointed i  guess this is a good case study for  the term well the the phrase yet the  trace of the true self exists in the  false self  because i guess that's true enough here  anyway let's move on there's one more  thing i want to show you guys  and no i'm still not letting you guys go  because there's one more thing  i want to showcase in the first video of  townscaper  i tried building some skyscrapers and  while i concluded that it's really not  meant for that kind of thing  and it usually even makes your game lag  a bit too much because those builds are  way bigger than the game is intended for  also you get these strange details in  the roofs and  planters and random clothes  hanging from wires between the buildings  all of that stuff  it's not really meant for this but at  the same time it's just too much fun  to build these things and i'm a big fan  of going against the game's intentions  so screw it let's just do it um and i  figured that  given the fact that we now have  perfectly round grids and also perfectly  square grids  as well which you can definitely find  especially if you look for those  lines of perfectly square grids that  just go across the map  you can now much better build  skyscrapers and  maybe just come up with a single  skyscraper design and see how that goes  it doesn't have to be too intricate  but it's uh something worth pointing out  so for this one for instance i was  trying to go something kind of patronus  towers inspired  except just one instead of twin towers  kind of post-modern with a big  well spire on top um  and yeah i think it kind of works and  also it's a good exercise of the  new graphic mode where you just  completely remove all of the textures  because it helps a little bit with  coming up with skyscrapers because you  don't have to deal with the weird colors  of the roofs anymore  or with the details like windows on the  walls um  so yeah all together i think it's still  a fun exercise to try and build  skyscrapers in the game and i know i'm  not the only person who has done this  i've seen  so many great skyscraper builds pop up  as well just figured  that everybody watching this should know  that this is a really fun thing that you  can do with the game as well and  especially now that we have the new grid  types  there are so many options for just  doodling about  with modernist architecture as well so  let's take a quick look at that  and then i promise the video is over  god i love that sound anyway here's our  rendered final building  uh before the windows are in when i  think it actually looks  a little bit better because as soon as  all of the windows start appearing  you notice that in reality this thing is  just a grotesquely  huge castle mess but um  now let's turn off the textures again  and see what that looks like i think for  kind of modern builds like this you can  actually play with the textureless  models  and especially see what kind of lighting  looks best on it because you can  definitely make things look pretty cool  as soon as you just get the  the right lighting so that's something  fun to play around with  and maybe you can even build some cities  from lord of the rings with this or  something like that  the last thing i want to show is that  you also have this sort of simplified  option i haven't seen many people make  use of it and  to be fair i'm actually not sure what to  call it i'm not an expert of these kinds  of things  but uh it's also there which is good to  note and you can make some  well simplified lighting-less versions  of your city with this as well  and i always find it fun to open up my  old saves  and just go through the new options and  see what they look like  actually let's just do that for the last  part of this video  i swear this video will never end on my  watch  anyway i hope you guys enjoyed this and  found it a good look into all of the new  stuff in townscaper  and if you have it or if you're still  looking to buy it  i highly recommend checking out all of  these new graphic options because  they're just really fun to play with  like anything in the game  there's not really that much of a point  to it but that's just the  the fun therapeutic doodling aspect  of it i suppose anyway i'll see you guys  in the next video of townscaper because  i  do imagine there are still some updates  to come so  whenever anything is getting added or i  get a weird random idea  i'm sure we'll find each other here  again bye guys
 

